        {
          "id": "start-info",
          "kind": "html",
          "title": "About this template",
          "x": 764,
          "y": 64,
          "width": 492,
          "height": 640,
          "sourceId": "main",
          "showHeader": false,
          "transparentBackground": true,
          "noBorder": true,
          "background": "transparent",
          "borderColor": "#d5dce8",
          "borderThickness": 0,
          "filters": [],
          "htmlData": {
            "sourceIds": [],
            "maxRows": 0,
            "useFilteredContext": true,
            "bindings": []
          },
          "htmlDocument": "<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}html,body{margin:0;background:transparent;color:#1d2939;font:13px/1.5 Segoe UI,system-ui,sans-serif}h1{margin:0;font-size:22px}p{margin:2px 0 0;color:#5d6b82}section{background:#fff;border:1px solid #d5dce8;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin-bottom:12px}h2{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:15px}ul{margin:0;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}.note{padding:10px 12px;border-radius:10px;background:#eef2fa;color:#5d6b82;font-size:12.5px}</style></head><body><section><h2>How it works</h2><p style=\"margin:0;color:inherit\">The <b>Budget</b> page is a Report Grid. Type amounts directly in the cells. The <b>Total</b> column and row are formulas, so they update by themselves.</p></section><section><h2>What you can change</h2><ul><li><b>Periods and departments</b> – the guide, or type in the grid.</li><li><b>Formats and colors</b> – select cells and use the format controls above the grid.</li><li><b>More rows</b> – right-click a row number to insert rows; check that the totals still cover them.</li></ul></section><div class=\"note\">This page is only for getting started. The last step in the guide removes it.</div></body></html>"
        },
